component cia402_homecomp "cia402 homing module";

description """
A homing module for cia402 devices, buildable with halcompile, that lets the
servo drive run its own CiA402 homing state machine (object 6098h) instead of
LinuxCNC jogging the joint to a switch.

\\fBHOMING_BASE\\fR below must point at the homing.c that ships with the
LinuxCNC install on \\fBthis\\fR machine (not the Windows dev box -- this file
is deployed to the LinuxCNC/EtherCAT PC and built there). Typical locations:
  /usr/include/linuxcnc/src/emc/motion/homing.c   (uspace deb install)
  ~/linuxcnc-dev/src/emc/motion/homing.c           (built from source)
Find it with: find / -name homing.c 2>/dev/null

Creates input hal pins joint.N.request-cia-homing that select the CIA homing
state machine for that joint (set from INI via CIA402_HOMING_ENABLED), and
output pin joint.N.is-cia-homing that confirms the selection. Joints that do
not request CIA homing fall through to the normal LinuxCNC homing.c behavior.

Install with: halcompile --install cia402_homecomp.comp
Then select it via: \\fB[EMCMOT]HOMEMOD=cia402_homecomp\\fR in the INI.

\\fBNote:\\fR halcompile is provided by the linuxcnc-uspace-dev package.
""";

pin out bit is_module = 1; // one pin is required to use halcompile)

license "GPL";
author "adapted from Collin Bardini's cia402_homecomp for the Benchman XT / Stepperonline A6 conversion";
option homemod;
option extra_setup;
;;

#define HOMING_BASE /home/cnc/linuxcnc-2.9.10/src/emc/motion/homing.c

#define STR(s) #s
#define XSTR(s) STR(s)

// Cycles the drive's homing-completion statusword bits must hold true, in a row,
// before we trust them and hand control back to normal motion. At SERVO_PERIOD=1ms
// this is ~100ms, matching the debounce cia402.comp itself uses for stat_homed.
#define CIA_SETTLE_CYCLES 100

#include "motion.h"
#include "homing.h"

static char *home_parms;
RTAPI_MP_STRING(home_parms, "Example home parms");

EXTRA_SETUP()
{
    rtapi_print_msg(RTAPI_MSG_ERR, "cia402_homecomp started\n");
    return 0;
}

